at: 'png'}). Return up to 4 PNGs per call, at most 4 MiB combined. Render sequentially in one callback, e.g. for (const slide of [0, 1, 2, 3]) { await presentation.render({slide}); }. Use fewer slides or a lower render scale if the batch is too large. PNG bytes are attached directly to this tool response after a successful operation; each preview creates no Page or Library asset and is not available from a later status lookup. Hydration may use temporary container cache files. Select the image_references needed for rendering or image byte reads and set hydrate_images=true; omit hydration for text/layout reads and edits. First inspect image metadata without hydration: async ({presentation}) => (await presentation.inspect({select: '$.slides[1].elements[*]', include: ['id', 'kind', 'asset', 'fillImage']})).records reads slide 2 image references. Include background, picture-fill and inherited layout/master images needed by the render too; ordinary slide image elements alone may be incomplete. An empty selection only works for an image-free document. Upload source images with upload_artifact_images first, then pass its references in image_references and insert them with slide.images.add({path: reference, ...}). You may edit then render up to 4 PNGs (4 MiB combined) sequentially in the same callback; previews are returned only after a successful edit and create no Page or Library asset. This tool is part of plugin `Pages`.

